<+>Documentation Format Guide (Role Docs)\r\n\r\nPurpose\r\n- Standardize the format for role‑specific docs in /docs (e.g., filehandler.txt).\r\n- Keep docs short, scannable, and focused on a single responsibility.\r\n\r\nGeneral rules\r\n- Plain text only.\r\n- Use short headings with Title Case.\r\n- Use dash bullets for lists.\r\n- Keep lines under ~90 characters when possible.\r\n- Avoid long paragraphs; prefer bullets.\r\n- No code blocks unless necessary for syntax or examples.\r\n- Class names and methods must match the allowed list in docs/readme.txt.\r\n\r\nRequired sections (in this order)\r\n1) Title\r\n- One line: the document name and owner (team or role).\r\n\r\n2) Responsibility\r\n- 2–5 bullets describing what this part owns and does not own.\r\n\r\n3) Inputs\r\n- What data/commands this part receives.\r\n\r\n4) Outputs\r\n- What data/commands this part returns or produces.\r\n\r\n5) Interface (proposed)\r\n- List classes and key methods or functions.\r\n- Keep method signatures short and language‑agnostic.\r\n\r\n6) Behavior\r\n- Bullet steps for normal flow.\r\n\r\n7) Error Handling\r\n- Expected errors and how they surface to other parts.\r\n\r\n8) Testing Ideas (TDD)\r\n- 3–6 test cases written as short bullets.\r\n\r\nOptional sections (use only if needed)\r\n- Data Layout\r\n- Dependencies\r\n- Notes\r\n\r\nExample (for LLMs to follow)\r\n\r\nTitle\r\nProgram Control Plan (Team C)\r\n\r\nResponsibility\r\n- Orchestrate program flow based on CLI arguments.\r\n- Call File Handler to list files or fetch file contents.\r\n- Pass raw content to Cipher (if enabled) and return readable output.\r\n- Do not access the file system directly.\r\n\r\nInputs\r\n- CLI arguments: [index], [optional key path].\r\n\r\nOutputs\r\n- Printed file list or decoded file contents.\r\n- User‑friendly error messages.\r\n\r\nInterface (proposed)\r\n- class ProgramController\r\n  - String listFiles()\r\n  - String showFile(int index, Optional<Path> keyPath)\r\n\r\nBehavior\r\n- If no args: list files and return numbered list.\r\n- If index provided: fetch file, optionally decipher, return content.\r\n\r\nError Handling\r\n- If index invalid: return \"Invalid file number\".\r\n- If file read fails: return \"Unable to read file\".\r\n- If cipher key invalid: return \"Invalid key\".\r\n\r\nTesting Ideas (TDD)\r\n- No args returns a numbered list.\r\n- Invalid index returns error message.\r\n- Valid index returns file content.\r\n- Invalid key returns error message.\r\n
