<+>User Interface Plan (Team A)\r\n\r\nResponsibility\r\n- Define valid command‑line inputs and outputs.\r\n- Display file lists, file contents, and error messages.\r\n- Do not read files directly or perform deciphering.\r\n\r\nInputs\r\n- CLI arguments: none, [fileNumber], or [fileNumber] [keyPath].\r\n\r\nOutputs\r\n- Numbered list of available files.\r\n- File contents (plain or deciphered).\r\n- User‑friendly error messages.\r\n\r\nInterface (proposed)\r\n- class TopSecret\r\n  - main(String[] args)\r\n  - ProgramController controller\r\n  \r\n\r\nBehavior\r\n- If no args: call ProgramController.listFiles() and print result.\r\n- If one arg: parse file number, call ProgramController.showFile(index, empty).\r\n- If two args: parse number and key path, call ProgramController.showFile(index, keyPath).\r\n- Print output and exit.\r\n\r\nError Handling\r\n- If arg count invalid: print \"Too many arguments\".\r\n- If file number invalid format: print \"Invalid file number\".\r\n- If file number out of range: print \"File number not found\".\r\n- If file cannot be read: print \"Unable to read file\".\r\n- If cipher key invalid or missing: print \"Invalid key\".\r\n\r\nTesting Ideas (TDD)\r\n- No args prints a numbered list.\r\n- One arg prints selected file content.\r\n- Two args uses alternate key path.\r\n- Invalid number format prints error.\r\n- Too many args prints error.\r\n
