<+>Cipher Decoding and Key Validation (Team D)\r\n\r\nResponsibility\r\n\r\n- Load cipher keys (default or user-provided) and validate the key mapping.\r\n- Decipher file contents using a validated CipherKey mapping.\r\n- Surface clear cipher-related errors (invalid key, missing key, bad format).\r\n- Do not read mission files or list directories (owned by File Handler).\r\n- Do not parse CLI args or print output (owned by UI / Program Control).\r\n\r\nInputs\r\n\r\n- Enciphered text content as a String (from ProgramController).\r\n- Optional keyPath as a String (from ProgramController) or default key location.\r\n- Key file content read as a String (provided by FileReaderService via ProgramController).\r\n\r\nOutputs\r\n\r\n- CipherKey object with mapping when key is valid.\r\n- Deciphered text as a String when ciphering is enabled and key is valid.\r\n- User-friendly error strings (or error signals) when key is invalid or decipher fails.\r\n\r\nInterface (proposed)\r\n\r\n- class CipherService\r\n\r\n  - CipherKey loadKey(String keyPath)\r\n  - String decipher(String input, CipherKey key)\r\n- class CipherKey\r\n\r\n  - Map<Character, Character> mapping\r\n  - boolean validate()\r\n\r\nBehavior\r\n\r\n- If ProgramController requests deciphering:\r\n\r\n  - Determine keyPath (use provided path if present, else default key path).\r\n  - Load key content (ProgramController uses FileReaderService; CipherService parses).\r\n  - Parse key content into mapping pairs (character-to-character).\r\n  - Build CipherKey and call validate().\r\n  - If valid: return CipherKey to ProgramController.\r\n- When decipher(input, key) is called:\r\n\r\n  - For each character in input:\r\n\r\n    - If character exists in key.mapping: replace using mapped value.\r\n    - Else: keep character unchanged (spaces, punctuation, newlines).\r\n  - Return the transformed (deciphered) output string.\r\n\r\nError Handling\r\n\r\n- Missing key file / unreadable key content: surface \"Invalid key\".\r\n- Key format invalid (unparseable lines, missing delimiter, empty mapping): \"Invalid key\".\r\n- Key validation fails (duplicate outputs, conflicting mappings, incomplete rules): \"Invalid key\".\r\n- Null/empty input to decipher: return empty string (no error).\r\n- If CipherKey is null or not validated before decipher: surface \"Invalid key\".\r\n\r\nTesting Ideas (TDD)\r\n\r\n- loadKey with default key path returns a validated CipherKey.\r\n- loadKey with a bad path or unreadable content results in \"Invalid key\".\r\n- loadKey rejects malformed key content (bad lines / missing pairs) with \"Invalid key\".\r\n- CipherKey.validate fails when mapping has duplicates or conflicts.\r\n- decipher replaces mapped letters and preserves punctuation/newlines unchanged.\r\n- decipher with valid key produces expected plaintext for a known ciphertext sample.\r\n
