<+>File Handler Plan (Team B)\r\n\r\nResponsibility\r\n- Own all direct file system access for data files.\r\n- Provide program control a clean API: list available files and return contents.\r\n- Keep data folder location flexible (project root /data or working‑dir /data).\r\n\r\nInputs\r\n- Requests to list files.\r\n- Requests to read a file by index or filename.\r\n\r\nOutputs\r\n- Sorted list of filenames.\r\n- Raw file contents as a String (via Optional).\r\n\r\nInterface (proposed)\r\n- class FileCatalog\r\n  - List<String> listFiles()\r\n  - Optional<String> getByIndex(int index)\r\n  - Optional<String> getByName(String filename)\r\n- class FileReaderService\r\n  - String readFile(String path) throws IOException\r\n\r\nBehavior\r\n- Resolve data directory in this order:\r\n  1) ./data (project root).\r\n  2) ./build/../data if running from build (fallback).\r\n  3) working‑dir/data (same folder as program).\r\n- If no data directory is found, warn on stderr and default to ./data.\r\n- listFiles() refreshes the cached list each call, returns sorted filenames\r\n  (case‑insensitive) without indices.\r\n- getByIndex() maps 1‑based input into the cached list and reads by filename.\r\n- getByName() builds a full path and reads the file contents.\r\n- readFile() returns raw file contents (no decipher here) or throws IOException\r\n  if the path is missing or a directory.\r\n\r\nError Handling\r\n- If data directory missing: print a warning; listFiles() may return empty.\r\n- If file cannot be read: log to stderr in FileCatalog and return Optional.empty().\r\n- FileReaderService throws IOException for missing paths or directories.\r\n\r\nTesting Ideas (TDD)\r\n- listFiles() on empty data dir returns empty list.\r\n- listFiles() returns sorted order without indices.\r\n- getByIndex() with invalid index returns empty Optional.\r\n- getByName() returns empty Optional on read error.\r\n- readFile() returns exact file contents or throws IOException.\r\n
