<+>Program Control Plan (Team C)\r\n\r\nResponsibility\r\n- Orchestrate program flow based on CLI arguments.\r\n- Request file lists and contents from the File Handler.\r\n- Pass raw content to Cipher (if enabled) and return readable output.\r\n- Do not access the file system directly.\r\n\r\nInputs\r\n- CLI arguments: [fileNumber], [optional keyPath].\r\n- File list and file contents from File Handler.\r\n- Cipher key path or content when ciphering is enabled.\r\n\r\nOutputs\r\n- Numbered list of available files.\r\n- File contents (plain or deciphered).\r\n- User‑friendly error messages.\r\n\r\nInterface (proposed)\r\n- class ProgramController\r\n  - String listFiles()\r\n  - String showFile(int index, Optional<String> keyPath)\r\n  - FileCatalog catalog\r\n  - FileReaderService reader\r\n  - CipherService cipher\r\n\r\nBehavior\r\n- If no args: request listFiles() from File Handler and format numbered list.\r\n- If fileNumber provided: fetch file by index, read contents.\r\n- If ciphering enabled: load key (default or provided) and decipher content.\r\n- Return output string to UI layer for printing.\r\n\r\nError Handling\r\n- If file list is empty: return \"No files available\".\r\n- If index invalid: return \"Invalid file number\".\r\n- If file read fails: return \"Unable to read file\".\r\n- If cipher key invalid or missing: return \"Invalid key\".\r\n\r\nTesting Ideas (TDD)\r\n- No args returns numbered list from File Handler.\r\n- Empty file list returns \"No files available\".\r\n- Invalid index returns error message.\r\n- Valid index returns file content.\r\n- Cipher enabled with valid key returns deciphered text.\r\n- Cipher enabled with invalid key returns error message.\r\n
